    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12041e16_62d0c38a",
        "filename": "board/eve/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 356,
      "author": {
        "id": 1269501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-01T00:09:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Why is MF preferred being ignored?\n\nChange is partially correcting `usb_mux_set()` call for DP AltMode compliance. Partially logic and nomenclature correction.\n\nNomenclature: Per DP VESA AltMode spec, `mf_pref` bit specifies the /preference/ of the dock. This preference is overridden by host\u0027s ultimate selection. Logic in `pd_dfp_dp_get_pin_mode()` drives this mf_sel.\n\nCompliance: DP AltMode dictates we place \"pins to be reconfigured\" into safe mode pre-Configure. And only mux them post-ACK. Previously we were muxing /all/ lanes at /Configure/ time. Also the fact we were taking out USB3 lanes inappropriately on PinD configure, as cited in b:139708494#comment6 . mf_sel logic compares to MultiFunction PinConfig states, accounting for DP deprecation of A,B,E,F.\n\nLogic: Was flawed in that a \"mf\u003d1, Pin\u003dC\" host would cause the mux to be set inappropriately despite \"Pin\u003dC\" being used. This is due to erroneous logic in `pd_dfp_dp_get_pin_mode()`. Described in `Table 5-7: DFP_U Pin Assignment Selection Mandates`.\n\n\u003e I\u0027d recommend using our updated implementation of these functions in the ToT version of usb_pd_alt_mode_dfp.c\n\nI am unsure how to cleanly \"cherry-pick\" the entire file. The patch series is quite lengthy, and was refactored multiple times. It is even a different file.\n\nHow should I approach this? Should I \"copy and paste\" the contents and say \"forklifting to ToT\"?",
      "parentUuid": "424f1ced_7ada9d2b",
      "revId": "f0e2ba120baa41398f6db95140aeb8bbc5386200",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
