    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0026e5a4_f23152c9",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/anx74xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1269501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-01T00:09:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Compliance + Logic.\n\nCompliance: To be robust, DP VESA spec dictates Generation threshold \u003e\u003e Detection threshold. Current code logic incorrectly uses \u003cdetection\u003e 2ms HPD IRQ debounce. We should be using \u003cgeneration\u003e 3ms HPD Level debounce per VESA spec.\n\nLogic: Resetting the chip /theoretically/ puts HPD into 44k PD Input mode. This may not be enough to discharge leakage currents. This low level ensures AP detects a full HPD disconnect prior to potentially Hi-Z\u0027ing the line by asserting RESET_L.\n\nAsserting a low firmly avoids phantom connections.",
      "parentUuid": "14b7206c_c1b165fd",
      "revId": "f0e2ba120baa41398f6db95140aeb8bbc5386200",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
